            //5th testimonial(No Ar,Kr,Ru,Sp,Por,It,Tr,De,Tw)
                [
                    'testimonials_id' => 5,
                    'languages_id' => '1',
                    'title' => 'Aayush - India',
                    'text' => 'Aayush is from Vadodara, Gujarat, India. He wanted to be an animator and artist so he came to America to study animation. In the U.S., Aayush decided to become a filmmaker in order to produce his own animated films. Four months ago he joined the Business/TOEIC program at MLI Hollywood to brushen up on his English skills. I spoke to Aayush today about ways he saves money in Los Angeles. Here’s what he has to say….
                    "Public transportation service in LA is pretty good. You can save money by getting a weekly or monthly metro pass, called a Tap card. Avoid ubers and taxis if you can.
                    For people who like to party, drink, or eat good food check out the website “eventbrite” for free or very cheap entry tickets to events, parties, and restaurants. I see a lot of movie premiers for free by signing up for the official websites of Warner Brothers and Gofobo. You can also get free tickets to T.V. show screenings like Jimmy Kimmel, Ellen Degeners and more on 1iota.com. You can also get “MoviePass” online for $10 a month which allows you to see unlimited movies at most theaters. Tekila Bar on Hollywood Walk of Fame near Yucca and Las Palmas have happy hour every day (where you can drink and eat cheaply). Every day there is a different deal in addition to the happy hour. If you like to bowl, check out “Pinz bowling” in Culver city. You pay $8 for unlimited bowling.
                    For shopping, I recommend going to “Miniso” on Hollywood Boulevard across from the Chinese theater. They sell good quality houseware, stationary, souvenirs, electronics and more at a very cheap price.
                    Enjoy Los Angeles!”',
                ],
                [
                    'testimonials_id' => 5,
                    'languages_id' => '5',
                    'title' => 'Aayush - India',
                    'text' => 'Aayush est originaire de Vadodara en Inde. Il est venu en Amérique pour étudier l’animation car il aimerait devenir un acteur, animateur. Aux États -Unie, Aayush a decidé de devenir producteur pour produire son propre film. Il y a 4 mois, il décida de prendre les cours de Business/TOEIC pour améliorer son anglais. Aujourd’hui, il aimerait donner des conseils sur comment economiser son argent.
