                    'title' => 'Cheapest ESL School in Los Angeles!',
                    'text' => 'Westwood Campus Featured Student

                    This week’s Featured Student is Touda from Morocco. She currently studies in our Advanced Conversation Program during the afternoon. In Morocco, she works as a journalist and takes additional journalism classes here in Los Angeles. In her free time, she likes to hike, go to the beach, and visit Universal Studios. Here’s what she had to say about MLI:
                    
                    “I started studying English in Los Angeles at UCLA extension. When I was studying there, I heard about MLI from a classmate. She recommended this school to me, so I came to check it out and decided to study English here. It’s a really good school and the cheapest ESL school in Los Angeles. UCLA extension is $6,500 per semester, which is just three months. That’s so expensive! My mom even joked that I must be a Moroccan princess because my classes there were so expensive. [Three months at MLI is just $1,200 for the afternoon conversation program]. Both schools are really close to each other in Westwood too, which is the neighborhood where I live. I love this neighborhood because it’s very student-centered with lots of international and native university students around. I’m taking the conversation program now, which really helps me improve my speaking skills for everyday life. If you want to improve your speaking, this is the best class to do it. I think if students really want to learn English, they should definitely come to study at MLI because it’s near UCLA, and is the cheapest ESL school in the area! I really love this school.”'
