                [
                    'testimonials_id' => 33,
                    'languages_id' => '12',
                    'title' => 'I chose MLI and I am really satisfied with my choice.(Esther | Korean,Japan)',
                    'text' => 'How did you choose MLI?
                    - First, I researched online. I saw there were so many schools in Los Angeles, especially in Koreatown. I saw they were cheap in Koreatown, but I heard they weren’t very good schools, so I decided not to go to them. I researched more and found MLI. I read many great reviews online about MLI, and I saw that many of the reviews were Japanese, which I liked because it would help me feel comfortable. Everything I saw about the school looked really good, and I heard Westwood was a great location, so I chose MLI and I am really satisfied with my choice.
                    
                    What’s the best thing about MLI?
                    - I think the teachers and staff are very kind and funny too. Also, there are many different nationalities in the school, so I can learn about many country’s culture, which makes it really interesting. I can compare things with them and think more internationally.
                    
                    What do you usually do during your free time?
                    - I have been volunteering to help out Lindsay, the Program Coordinator at school. I help her organize and handle paperwork. I volunteered so that I could improve my conversation skills and practice using English, and it’s been really helpful. Also, when I’m not at school, I like to just relax at home and go out with my friends to new restaurants or sightseeing.
                    
                    What do you like about Los Angeles?
                    - The weather is always nice. I really like the people here because they always are friendly. If I say “Hi” or anything like that, they always respond kindly and say things like “Have a nice day.” I like that it’s so positive.
                    
                    Do you have any tips or recommendations for students considering moving to LA to study at MLI?
